{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>טובם</b> — an epithet, like <b>מתו</b> (his terror), which is in construct state and is a participle standing as a noun." "<b>ישר ממסוכה</b> — more difficult than a hedge of thorns, and the samekh is like shin." "<b>וטעם יום מצפיך</b> — behold, the day concerning which your watchmen call has come; your visitation has arrived now, swiftly may it be." "<b>מבוכתם</b> — their confusion, and the mem reverts to the prince, the judge, and the great one."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra cites Genesis 9:2 where מֵטֶם is paired with יִרְאַתְכֶם; he calls it סמוך (construct) and פועל עומד (participle functioning as noun). The lemma head follows his own text.", 1 "Reading ממסוכה as ממשוכת with samekh replacing shin; the comparison is to a thorn-hedge.", 3 "Ibn Ezra explains the suffix mem on מבוכתם as referring back to the dignitaries mentioned earlier in the verse."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:24.119202302Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}